{% comment %}
  The large line-art illustration for one spice, built from Santosh's
  "KCC Website Aromatics" sheet by scripts/build-ingredient-art.py.

  Every one is a scatter of the whole spice drawn at a matched scale, so the
  line weight reads the same from one to the next - a cinnamon stick is still
  bigger than a carom seed, but the pen that drew them is the same width. That
  only holds if they all share one box, which is why there is no per-spice
  ratio table here any more: the build script pads all nine to the same
  viewBox, centred on each drawing's own ink.

  They carry the brand brown as a fill on the root, since an <img> can't
  inherit currentColor.

  Keyed on the spice's display name, matching ingredient-icon.liquid's mapping
  so a block only has to be named once.

  Accepts:
    name       - the spice's display name, e.g. 'Black pepper'
    class_name - class for the <img>
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign key = name | default: '' | handle
  assign art = ''

  case key
    when 'ginger'
      assign art = 'ingredient-art-ginger.svg'
    when 'cardamom', 'green-cardamom'
      assign art = 'ingredient-art-cardamom.svg'
    when 'cinnamon', 'cinnamon-stick', 'cinnamon-sticks'
      assign art = 'ingredient-art-cinnamon.svg'
    when 'cloves', 'clove'
      assign art = 'ingredient-art-cloves.svg'
    when 'black-pepper', 'pepper', 'peppercorn', 'peppercorns'
      assign art = 'ingredient-art-pepper.svg'
    when 'fennel', 'fennel-seeds', 'carom', 'carom-seeds', 'ajwain', 'carom-seeds-ajwain'
      assign art = 'ingredient-art-carom.svg'
    when 'star-anise', 'anise'
      assign art = 'ingredient-art-star-anise.svg'
    when 'coffee-bean', 'coffee-beans', 'coffee'
      assign art = 'ingredient-art-coffee.svg'
    when 'tea-leaf', 'tea-leaves', 'black-tea', 'tea'
      assign art = 'ingredient-art-tea.svg'
  endcase
-%}

{%- if art != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The shared box the build script pads every drawing to. Hardcoded rather
    than per-spice so the layout can't jump as one loads, and so a spice whose
    ink happens to be narrower isn't magnified more than its neighbours.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <img
    class="{{ class_name }}"
    src="{{ art | asset_url }}"
    alt="{{ name | escape }}"
    width="1603"
    height="1106"
    loading="lazy"
  >
{%- endif -%}
